From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:19:58 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 179/182] hjviewer: Cargo.lock takes crossbeam-channel 0.5.15
 and upstream's rustls-webpki and webpki-roots

crossbeam-channel 0.5.13 has a double free when a channel is dropped
(RUSTSEC-2025-0024); flexi_logger in hbb_common uses it for the log
writer on every platform, the PC's SYSTEM service included. 0.5.15 is
the fixed release and HJViewer's own choice: upstream master still pins
0.5.13. rustls-webpki 0.103.16 and webpki-roots 1.0.11 are the
certificate path validation and the Mozilla root store of the TLS
connections that verify with them (the wss:// signaling and relay among
them). rustls-webpki 0.103.16 needs rustls-pki-types >= 1.12 (1.15.1, as
upstream), which now also depends on zeroize (already in the lock).

Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk 3202d1764c58902db8c97d803f1f63fa7cbf9e45 (chore(deps): update webpki-roots and rustls-webpki in Cargo.lock (#16639))
Backported from rustdesk/rustdesk f96a44a0190e5e5ad79ceed298efbbc7a58a03db (chore: update webpki-roots to latest Mozilla root store (#16713))
Against upstream: each package moved alone with cargo +1.75.0 update -p
<name>@<old> --precise <new>, so nothing else re-resolves; the
lock diff is these four packages and the webpki-roots references.
Upstream's webpki-root-certs 1.0.3 -> 1.0.10 is not taken (not one of
the crates this change is for). All build with Rust 1.75
(rustls-webpki declares rust-version 1.71, rustls-pki-types 1.60).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
